    {domain:'precision',difficulty:'foundation',q:'Choose the grammatically correct sentence.',options:['Each of the students are responsible for the file.','Each of the students is responsible for the file.','Each of the student is responsible for the file.','Each students are responsible for the file.'],answer:1,errors:['grammar','','grammar','grammar'],explanation:'The subject is Each, which is singular, so the verb is is. Students is plural only because it follows of the.'},
    {domain:'comprehension',difficulty:'foundation',q:'A library extended its evening hours after students requested more study time. Attendance increased during the new hours.\n\nWhich statement best summarises the passage?',options:['Students prefer studying only at night.','Longer evening access was followed by higher attendance.','The library should remain open all night.','Attendance increased before the hours changed.'],answer:1,errors:['overreach','','overreach','detail'],explanation:'The passage states that evening hours were extended and attendance then increased. It does not say students study only at night or recommend all-night opening.'},
